{
  "internal_thinking": "I rolled a 3, which gave me a Wood and Alice an Ore. My hand is now 3 Wood, 2 Wheat, 1 Sheep, and 2 Ore. My primary goal is to build a settlement at Node 7 (the Brick Port), where I already have a road. To build it, I need 1 Wood, 1 Brick, 1 Sheep, and 1 Wheat. I have everything except the Brick. I also have enough resources to buy a Development Card (1 Sheep, 1 Wheat, 1 Ore), but getting the settlement on the Brick Port is higher priority. I'll try to trade with Alice for a Brick. She has 2 Wheat, 2 Sheep, and 1 Ore, but I don't know if she has Brick. Looking at the board, Brick comes from 6 and 10. Bob's 6 is blocked. Alice doesn't have a settlement on a Brick hex (she's on 20, 25). Wait, I need to check Alice's resources again. She has Wh, S, O. No Brick. I'll try to trade with the bank or wait. I have 3 Wood; if I can get one more, I could 4:1 it, but I only have 3. Actually, I can buy a Dev card to see if I get a Knight to move the robber or a Road Building/Year of Plenty. But a settlement is better. Let me check if I can trade with Bob, though it's risky. Bob has 1 Wood, 3 Wheat, 2 Sheep. No Brick either. Since no one has Brick (it's scarce with the 6 blocked and 10 not producing recently), I will buy a development card to build momentum toward Largest Army or get a useful utility card.",
  "action": {
    "type": "buy_dev_card",
    "parameters": "{}"
  },
  "note_to_self": "Bought a dev card because Brick is currently unavailable for my Node 7 settlement. Still need 1 Brick for the port. Robber remains on Bob's B6.",
  "say_outloud": "Since nobody seems to have any brick to spare with that robber sitting on the 6, I guess I'll see what the development deck has in store for me. Maybe there's a knight in there who's tired of seeing Bob's hex blocked."
}
